---
title: Vue library
description: The GateKeeper Vue 3 package — a public SPA client exposed as a plugin and a composable.
section: Application libraries
---

`@gatekeeper/vue` is the Vue 3 integration for GateKeeper. It wraps the framework-agnostic
`@gatekeeper/spa-oauth` public client in a Vue plugin and a `useGateKeeper()` composable that
exposes reactive auth state.

The package source lives at `packages/gatekeeper-vue`; a runnable example is at `frontends/vue`.

## Requires a public OAuth client

Vue SPAs run in the browser, so they must use a **public** OAuth client:

- `client_type: "public"` — **no client secret**.
- PKCE S256 is the only client protection.
- Tokens live in `sessionStorage` and are exposed to XSS by design.
- Add the app origin to the server's `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (it calls `/oauth/token` and
  `/oauth/userinfo` directly).

Prefer a confidential BFF whenever the framework has a server runtime.

## Install the plugin

```ts
import { createApp } from 'vue';
import { createGateKeeper } from '@gatekeeper/vue';
import App from './App.vue';

createApp(App)
	.use(
		createGateKeeper({
			config: {
				idpBaseUrl: import.meta.env.VITE_GATEKEEPER_IDP_BASE_URL,
				authUiBaseUrl: import.meta.env.VITE_GATEKEEPER_AUTH_UI_BASE_URL,
				tenantId: import.meta.env.VITE_GATEKEEPER_TENANT_ID,
				clientId: import.meta.env.VITE_GATEKEEPER_CLIENT_ID,
				redirectUri: `${window.location.origin}/`,
				scope: 'openid profile email'
			}
		})
	)
	.mount('#app');
```

Only the public `clientId` is configured — no secret. The plugin builds the client, keeps a
`shallowRef` of its snapshot, and finishes the redirect on mount when the URL carries `?code=`.
Pass `handleRedirectCallback: false` to disable that, or `client` to supply a pre-built client.

## Use the composable

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import { useGateKeeper } from '@gatekeeper/vue';

const { isAuthenticated, user, expiresAt, error, signIn, signOut, refresh, getAccessToken } =
	useGateKeeper();
</script>

<template>
	<button v-if="!isAuthenticated" @click="signIn()">Sign in</button>
	<template v-else>
		<p>Signed in as {{ user?.email ?? user?.sub }}</p>
		<button @click="signOut()">Sign out</button>
	</template>
</template>
```

`useGateKeeper()` returns `computed` refs — `status`, `isAuthenticated`, `isLoading`, `user`,
`expiresAt`, `error` — plus the actions `signIn`, `signOut`, `refresh`, `getAccessToken`, and the
raw `client`. Because the values are `computed`, templates and watchers update automatically.

## Sign-in / sign-out flow

1. **Sign in** — `signIn()` mints PKCE, stashes the transaction, and redirects to
   `{AUTH_UI_BASE_URL}/auth/{clientId}/sign-in?...`.
2. **Callback** — the plugin exchanges `?code=` for tokens and strips the params.
3. **Refresh** — `getAccessToken()`/`refresh()` rotate the refresh token before expiry.
4. **Sign out** — clears `sessionStorage` (no server-side logout endpoint).

## Fetch userinfo

```ts
const claims = await client.fetchUserInfo(); // GET /oauth/userinfo?tenant_id=... (Bearer)
```

## Example app

`frontends/vue` is a Vite + Vue 3 SPA (dev port 5176). Register a public client with
`frontends/vue/scripts/register-public-client.sh`, paste the output into `.env`, add
`http://localhost:5176` to `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`, then `npm install && npm run dev`.
